{
    "notes": [
        "Local synthetic Caddy HTTP/1.1 on one physical host; disjoint CPU allocations do not remove shared-host variability. No TLS/WAN and no production capacity guarantee.",
        "Candidate ran first, then control, once each. Both use two SSE workers, sixteen generator shards, 90-second phases, thirty writes and a halfway reconnect. Control includes lazy legacy encoding but restores per-delivery metric label lookup.",
        "All writes and initial/reconnect handshakes completed with zero public GETs, no HTTP/SSE errors, stale final views or failed/pending jobs.",
        "Both overall results remain false: 10,000-viewer push p95 exceeds 100 ms and compact phases have no live-GET latency samples. Control also exceeds the push target at 1,000 viewers.",
        "Candidate 1,000/10,000-viewer published-update p95: 42.35/556.67 ms. Control: 120.71/507.51 ms. These single runs do not establish an end-to-end latency benefit from cached labels.",
        "An isolated nine-repeat counter experiment measured median 235.59 ms for 100,000 label-lookup-plus-increment operations versus 59.94 ms for increments on a cached child. This excludes network, ASGI and application work; it is not a delivery-latency benchmark."
    ],
